bedivere: [i]Damn guests... what's wrong with dial-up?[/i]
bedivere: Huh? Percival? You're not supposed to be here... at all. What's going on?
A king fisher brought me back. I guess it was time.
bedivere: Guess so.
What have you been doing here?
bedivere: Upkeep, mostly. This place was a church first before it was a hotel. I’m not sure why it changed that way. It seems in poor taste to me.
bedivere: Anyway, apparently internet's gotten better, so I'm redoing the wiring. Some beast in the walls keeps chewing it up anyway, so I may as well update it while I fix it.
I'm sorry to distract you, then, but Gawain said you could help me repair my sword?
bedivere: Goodness - I could, but I'm supposed to be working for the paying guests.
What kind of vermin? Maybe I could help free up your time.
bedivere: That's the thing.